Editor’s note: This story will be updated.

The highly-awaited 2026 Billboard Latin Music Week has officially kicked off with a wave of star-studded panels and showcases.&nbsp;

Running from Oct. 19 (today) to Oct. 22 at the Faena Forum and Faena Theater in Miami Beach, the weeklong music event began as early as 9 a.m. ET with welcome remarks from Leila Cobo, Co-Chief Content Officer at Billboard .&nbsp;

In true Latin Music Week fashion, Monday’s programming is, for the most part, dedicated to key business and industry conversations, which this year include Luminate’s CEO Rob Jonas talking about the state of Spanish-language music by the numbers, and a keynote conversation with music mogul Tommy Mottola and Alex Gallardo, President at Sony Music U.S. Latin on the rise of Latin music, globally.

