Additionally, attendees learned how to translate a 15-second viral clip into a sustainable community in the “Beyond the Algorithm: From Viral Moment to Global Fanbase” panel, as well as how the world’s fourth-largest music market is finding a global audience for its music in Portuguese in the “Brazil on the Rise: The Sound, Scale & Future of Brazilian Music” panel.

Monday’s roster also included a handful of star-studded conversations: Grupo Frontera talking about its international expansion; Kany García on the stories behind her biggest hits; the revival of salsa music with Tito Nieves and Luis Figueroa; and Quevedo and Kidd Voodoo joining forces on “The New Urban Movement” panel.

The 2026 Billboard Latin Music Week coincides with the 2026 Billboard Latin Music Awards, set to air Thursday, Oct. 22 from the James L. Knight Center in Miami on Telemundo and Peacock.

